WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:03.940
- The reason why there's
such division, right now,

00:00:03.940 --> 00:00:06.910
is because people want
people to go for the jugular,

00:00:06.910 --> 00:00:09.030
and because people, you know,

00:00:09.030 --> 00:00:10.500
are like, okay don't talk about it.

00:00:10.500 --> 00:00:11.570
It's either under rug swept,

00:00:11.570 --> 00:00:12.970
or it's just cut 'em at the throat.

00:00:12.970 --> 00:00:13.930
Like and it's like,

00:00:13.930 --> 00:00:16.760
the reason why that
division, I feel exists,

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:19.940
is because we're not focused
on the real root of the issues,

00:00:19.940 --> 00:00:22.540
and instead of just
talking about something

00:00:22.540 --> 00:00:23.373
that is right there

00:00:23.373 --> 00:00:26.070
that we can all talk about and
all join in the conversation,

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.450
and all feel like you're
a part of it, like,

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:29.360
instead of doing that,

00:00:29.360 --> 00:00:31.210
which is what I feel like your film did,

00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:33.790
everybody always wants to make some expose

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:37.730
that just murders people, and
it's like, that's not working.

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:40.400
Like, that kind of
mentality isn't working.

00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:42.360
- Hey man, I did it for a living!

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:43.960
I did it, you know.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:45.390
- But it's not working right now, like-

00:00:45.390 --> 00:00:46.340
- No, I don't think it is.

00:00:46.340 --> 00:00:48.540
- Fight people with that kind of,

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:49.820
you're not going to win at this point.

00:00:49.820 --> 00:00:51.748
Everybody keeps trying to do
that, and it's not working.

00:00:51.748 --> 00:00:52.870
- Right. Well it's permanent, also,

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:53.930
we never get a break, you know,

00:00:53.930 --> 00:00:57.460
What I realized is, to some extent,

00:00:57.460 --> 00:00:59.960
we as a country need makeup sex,

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:02.618
and I think when you're in
a permanent election cycle-

00:01:02.618 --> 00:01:03.451
- [Kelly] Don't we all? (laughing)

00:01:03.451 --> 00:01:06.690
- Yeah, the permanent election cycle,

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:10.950
really does set those
divisions in concrete.

00:01:10.950 --> 00:01:14.010
You never get a chance to
take off your team jersey,

00:01:14.010 --> 00:01:15.940
and kind of see people for who they are.

00:01:15.940 --> 00:01:19.000
And it's why, in this moment, I feel like,

00:01:19.000 --> 00:01:23.140
there's something important
happening, is that...

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:24.910
nobody likes to get called
out on their (beep),

00:01:24.910 --> 00:01:27.610
and I'm, you know, I always
had a terrible problem

00:01:27.610 --> 00:01:30.170
of being very defensive
about things like that,

00:01:30.170 --> 00:01:35.170
and I worked really hard to
try to be less that, but...

00:01:36.390 --> 00:01:39.800
it's a moment where we
might have a chance,

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:41.320
to see each other.

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:43.220
It's gonna be a hard conversation,

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:44.530
and it's going to take, you know,

00:01:44.530 --> 00:01:46.870
truth and reconciliation,

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:49.660
is a really difficult
place to be in a society,

00:01:49.660 --> 00:01:54.660
but if we don't address this,
truly gaping, open wound,

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.310
it won't ever heal,

00:01:57.310 --> 00:01:58.950
and we can pretend that,

00:01:58.950 --> 00:02:00.640
we're supposed to have two Americas,

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.647
but we're really not.

00:02:01.647 --> 00:02:04.210
It's okay, we're not all
supposed to get along

00:02:04.210 --> 00:02:05.043
and hold hands,

00:02:05.043 --> 00:02:06.550
and there will be real divisions,

00:02:06.550 --> 00:02:09.283
and real challenges, and real issues.

